Compile command gcc -o forkExample forkExample.c

Start-up: ./forkExample

	/* fork another process */
	This section uses fork() to create a new child process. The program then checks the result of fork() to determine what process it is running.

	/* child process */
	This section contains the code that runs in the child process. In this example, the child uses execlp() to run the ls command
	else if (pid == 0) {any code that calls on the method you want the child to do}

	/* parent process */
	This section contains the code that runs in the original parent process. The parent waits for the child to finish and then continues with the rest of the program.

